msgstr "Catatan Benchmark {#benchmark-notes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The above results were obtained on the `ibm_marrakesh` Heron r2 processor with default options and `use_session` enabled. For the `sloane_2dc_128` instance, `total_shots=12500` was used.\n"
msgstr "Hasil di atas diperoleh pada prosesor Heron r2 `ibm_marrakesh` dengan opsi default dan `use_session` diaktifkan. Untuk instance `sloane_2dc_128`, digunakan `total_shots=12500`.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-10-01
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reduced qubit count for MIS instances (74 and 124 versus 128 and 186 variables) reflects variable fixing in preprocessing.\n"
msgstr "Jumlah qubit yang berkurang untuk instance MIS (74 dan 124 dibandingkan dengan 128 dan 186 variabel) mencerminkan penetapan nilai variabel pada tahap preprocessing.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The problem instances for MIS are taken from the [Quantum Optimization Benchmarking Library](https://doi.org/10.1038/s43588-026-00991-1). - The instance for the Max-$k$-Cut problem is the [Zachary Karate Club graph](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zachary%27s_karate_club), which has a chromatic number of 5.\n"
msgstr "Instance masalah untuk MIS diambil dari [Quantum Optimization Benchmarking Library](https://doi.org/10.1038/s43588-026-00991-1). - Instance untuk masalah Max-$k$-Cut adalah [graf Zachary Karate Club](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zachary%27s_karate_club), yang memiliki bilangan kromatik 5.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "A note on QPU time {#a-note-on-qpu-time}"
msgstr "Catatan tentang waktu QPU {#a-note-on-qpu-time}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The QPU time a function run needs depends strongly on the chosen options, the number of warm-start iterations, and shots. With the default options, the function needs considerably less QPU time than standard QAOA, because it uses iterative warm-starting instead of a variational parameter training loop on the QPU.\n"
msgstr "Waktu QPU yang dibutuhkan satu run function sangat bergantung pada opsi yang dipilih, jumlah iterasi warm-start, dan shot. Dengan opsi default, function ini membutuhkan waktu QPU yang jauh lebih sedikit daripada QAOA standar, karena memakai warm-starting iteratif alih-alih loop pelatihan parameter variasional di QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As an example, both approaches were compared  on `ibm_phoenix` using Maximum Independent Set instances that correspond to function sizes `M` and `L`. A [standard QAOA workflow](/tutorials/quantum-approximate-optimization-algorithm) needed about 130 and 200 seconds of QPU time, respectively. The function with default options needed about 30 seconds in both cases. Results for other problems and settings will differ.\n"
msgstr "Sebagai contoh, kedua pendekatan dibandingkan  pada `ibm_phoenix` menggunakan instance Maximum Independent Set yang sesuai dengan ukuran function `M` dan `L`. [Workflow QAOA standar](/tutorials/quantum-approximate-optimization-algorithm) membutuhkan sekitar 130 dan 200 detik waktu QPU. Function dengan opsi default membutuhkan sekitar 30 detik pada kedua kasus. Hasil untuk masalah dan pengaturan lain akan berbeda.\n"

